The polygonal site has an approximately 98.5-metre southern side, but only approximately five-metre and four-metre sections adjoin the road. It does not have 98.5 metres of continuous road frontage. Depth is approximately 56 metres. SAM describes Laem Thong Road as public, with approximately 12 metres of carriageway and a 14-metre right of way. Orange planning zoning and residential/commercial surroundings are reported.

Registered acquisition identifies a three-storey shophouse numbered 138/18; the physical survey found three storeys plus a mezzanine. SAM also reports other structures without evidence confirming whether they legally form part of the land. Transfer follows only the property inventory that SAM acquired by registration. Check building registration, plans, permits and rights to other structures.

The source plan shows a large rear land parcel and narrow connections to the road, with the identified building separately marked. Confirm every title boundary, both access sections, access rights and the exact building included with SAM and the land office.

Travel from Pattaya toward Chon Buri on Sukhumvit Road (Highway 3), passing Harbor Mall and Vibharam Laemchabang Hospital. Enter Laem Thong Road on the right, passing Si Mum Mueang Laem Chabang Market, for approximately 1.3 kilometres; the property is on the left. Source-listed nearby places are Wat Laem Thong, Wat Laem Chabang and Laem Chabang Municipality School.

SAM showed direct-purchase status and this price on 11 September 2026. Contact 02-686-1888, sales@sam.or.th or LINE @samline, quoting 1P0017, to confirm availability, current price, viewing and terms. Administrator coordinates are used.

